  "scope": "Offline successful /prepaid/balance and /usage replies. Input key and team literals synthetic; no account data, external traffic or mutations. No product source changes.",
  "method": "Existing release QuickJS runtime and core object files linked into isolated macOS executables, exactly one GET, one POST and byte-identical request information. Candidate optimistically assumes injected response status/body has passed transport limits. Rust calculates cents, per-day time-series, sorted chart, sum and partial flag. JS retains toFixed(2), labels, snapshot mapping and legacy error/fallback. Isolated transport independently builds private marker headers and copies Rust result bytes. Program additionally compares warmed medians after three startup rounds with matched sides. Samples cover both full setup and result delivery. Rosetta for x86_64.",
