  "reason": "The official request already requests SUM(usd) per day with no dimensions for 30 days. 0-8-point end-to-end cases were usually neutral/slower, 30 points saved microseconds. Large 120/960 synthetic duplicate series benefit, but are outside the ordinary one-row-per-day shape. A production compatibility wrapper has two render branches plus trusted metadata, an envelope copy, and explicit filtering of unusual inputs. A new credential/transport path is not warranted.",
  "limitations": [
    "Synthetic response size distribution, no live service or customer data.",
    "The valid-path feasibility prototype can fall back for unsupported numeric/date representations. It does not implement the complete pre/post headers/size/error/cancellation policy needed for a replacement transport; the current application retains that policy.",
    "No release or cloud changes. Other profiles, signed delivery, Windows and remote service latency were not measured."
  ],
